# Hammer and Sickle — Unity project repository.
#
# POLICY CHANGED 2026-07-27: OPT-OUT. Everything is tracked unless it appears below.
# The previous policy was opt-in (`*` then `!*.cs`), which tracked 210 source files and
# nothing else — no .meta, no ProjectSettings, no scenes. That repo could not rebuild a
# working project: a clone regenerates every GUID, so all prefab/scene -> script
# references break, and the Unity layer setup (layer 7 / NoVolumeRendering, sorting
# layers), the Script Execution Order list and every Inspector wiring were unbacked.
#
# It also failed the same way an unassigned click-through slot does: SILENTLY, by
# omission. A new file type was simply never tracked and nothing said so. Opt-out fails
# loudly instead — unwanted files appear in `git status` where they can be seen.

