# --- GENERATED ASSETS — rebuilt by Editor tools, must NEVER be committed --
# TerrainArray_MiddleEast.asset is 288 MB and TestArray_RGB.asset is 8 MB. GitHub
# HARD-REJECTS any single file over 100 MB, so the terrain array cannot go into plain
# git at all, and putting it in LFS would burn ~29% of the 1 GB free quota per revision.
# Both are outputs of Assets/Editor/Chunked:
#   TerrainArray_* <- TextureArrayBuilder      (terrain PNGs in Assets/Art/HexTiles)
#   TestArray_*    <- HexBlendTestAssetBuilder (Phase 1 POC assets)
# ⚠ REBUILD STEP AFTER A FRESH CLONE — see Claude_Project §3.5c. The rebuilt asset gets
# a NEW GUID, so anything holding a serialized reference to it must be re-pointed.
/Assets/Resources/Chunked/TerrainArray_*.asset
/Assets/Resources/Chunked/TerrainArray_*.asset.meta
/Assets/Resources/Chunked/TestArray_*.asset
/Assets/Resources/Chunked/TestArray_*.asset.meta

# --- NOT ignored, deliberately, against the obvious instinct --------------
# Assets/Generated Data/  — scenario CONTENT, not build output. There are TWO load
#   paths and ScenarioManifest exposes a method family for each:
#     campaign   -> GetMapFilePath_GDP() etc -> AppService.GDP_*   -> THIS folder
#     standalone -> GetMapFilePath()     etc -> AppService.MapPath -> Documents/
#                                                My Games/Hammer and Sickle/scenario data
#   MapLoader picks between them (MapLoader.cs:47/:60), as does BattleManager for the
#   OOB (LoadCampaignOob vs LoadStandaloneOob). So this folder is the CAMPAIGN content.
#   It grows with the campaign, but it is text JSON; if .map files ever get heavy, add
#   them to LFS in .gitattributes rather than dropping them from the repo.
#   ⚠ THE STANDALONE CONTENT IN Documents/ IS STILL UNVERSIONED, and as of 2026-07-27
#   it is NEWER than the copies here (Khost.map 1,056 KB / 24 Jun 2026 vs 968 KB /
#   12 Nov 2025). Unresolved — see Claude_TODO.
# Packages/            — manifest.json, packages-lock.json AND the extracted NuGet
#   dependencies Main.asmdef compiles against. Without them a clone does not build.
